1. Fake assertions about the effectiveness of different birth control methods could include that the condom is the most effective at 76% and the birth control pill is only 57%;
2. False statements claiming that certain birth control methods are safer than others;
3. Fake assertions suggesting that certain birth control costs as little as $2 per month; and
4. Rhetorical questions asking if students know what the long-term effects of certain birth control methods are.
